20260529.113505.051 [<ideas.........] [The malvin gate-loop requires two consecutive sessions with `## KPOP_SOLVED` and passing gates to exit early. After g1 wrote]
20260529.113505.384 [<ideas.........] [KPOP_SOLVED, malvin immediately started g2 at 112916, just three seconds later. The quality_gates.log is empty, suggesting]
20260529.113505.670 [<ideas.........] [gates may not have been re-run or logged. The kpop.log indicates retry due to failed quality gates after the previous]
20260529.113507.904 [<ideas.........] [KPOP_SOLVED session. Additionally, g1 ran `cargo clippy` from the repo root without changing directories to `rust`.]
20260529.113508.141 [<ideas.........] [malvin's checks file specifies running `cd rust && cargo clippy` from the rust directory, but g1 executed `cargo clippy`]
20260529.113508.345 [<ideas.........] [from the repo root instead. g1s gate run at line 353 took 128 seconds, exited with 0, but was marked with an error symbol,]
20260529.113508.557 [<ideas.........] [which is unusual. During `make test`, the sandbox showed 986 MiB RSS and 10 processes. malvin reported that the workspace]
20260529.113508.773 [<ideas.........] [quality gates did not pass after the kpop session and retried due to failing gates after the previous `## KPOP_SOLVED`]
20260529.113510.016 [<ideas.........] [session. Notably, malvin requires two consecutive `KPOP_SOLVED` sessions with passing gates to exit early.]
20260529.113510.213 [<ideas.........] [The retry after g1 KPOP_SOLVED likely occurred because malvin requires two consecutive KPOP_SOLVED sessions with passing]
20260529.113510.427 [<ideas.........] [gates to exit early, and g1 was only the first session. Additionally, the empty quality_gates.log suggests gates may not]
20260529.113510.636 [<ideas.........] [have been re-run or logged properly, and there was a possible cwd mismatch where `cargo clippy` was executed from the repo]
20260529.113512.182 [<ideas.........] [root instead of the rust directory.]
20260529.113512.335 [<ideas.........] [After the first KPOP_SOLVED, malvin continues to a second session unless gates pass on that check. The early exit]
20260529.113512.494 [<ideas.........] [requirement of two consecutive KPOP_SOLVED sessions with passing gates means that even if gates pass after the first]
20260529.113512.688 [<ideas.........] [KPOP_SOLVED, malvin still runs g2 to achieve the second consecutive KPOP_SOLVED. This behavior is by design, not due to]
20260529.113515.200 [<ideas.........] [failure.]
20260529.113515.425 [<ideas.........] [However, the retry message states that quality gates did not pass after the previous ## KPOP_SOLVED session, implying the]
20260529.113515.597 [<ideas.........] [gates failed rather than indicating a need for another session. ]
20260529.113515.625 [<ideas.........] [Looking at the timeline closely:]
20260529.113515.719 [<ideas.........] [- 112912.753 - g1 finishes with all gates green]
20260529.113515.775 [<ideas.........] [- 112913.061 - KPOP_LOG written for g1]
20260529.113515.873 [<ideas.........] [- 112916.472 - g2 kpop session starts (~3.4 seconds later)]
20260529.113518.096 [<ideas.........] [Between these times, malvin likely executed quality gates, yet the quality_gates.log remains empty, which is suspicious.]
20260529.113518.407 [<ideas.........] [g1 completed its full gate suite at 112904, claimed pass at 112908, and logged KPOP_SOLVED at ~112913. Malvin then ran its]
20260529.113518.732 [<ideas.........] [own gate check between 112913 and 112916, before starting g2 at 112916. The quality_gates.log remained empty, possibly]
20260529.113520.968 [<ideas.........] [because malvin only writes to it during the initial check, not the post-session recheck.]
