20260529.113731.807 [<ideas.........] # MBC2: Why malvin gate-loop retries after `KPOP_SOLVED` when agent-reported gates pass
20260529.113732.619 [<ideas.........] The formal system here is unchanged: malvin `tidy` runs `.malvin/checks` sequentially, KPop agents log to
20260529.113733.306 [<ideas.........] `_kpop/exp_log_*_gN.md`, and the outer gate loop continues until malvin's own gate runner agrees (or until the loop budget
20260529.113733.600 [<ideas.........] is exhausted). Agent stdout claims are not part of that contract.
20260529.113734.442 [<ideas.........] **Evidence from this run** (`20260529_152109_3ajb6fp9`): g1 wrote `## KPOP_SOLVED` at ~11:29:13; g2's prompt at ~11:29:16
20260529.113734.927 [<ideas.........] already says `Retry: yes — quality gates did not pass after previous ## KPOP_SOLVED session`; `quality_gates.log` is 0 bytes
20260529.113735.744 [<ideas.........] for the entire run; initial malvin gate run stopped at clippy (~3.6s) and never reached `make test`; g1's self-check of all
20260529.113735.792 [<ideas.........] gates took ~128s.
20260529.113735.840 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.113735.930 [<ideas.........] ## Core assumptions (shared)
20260529.113736.189 [<ideas.........] | Assumption | Extreme limit | Negation | Pathological edge |
20260529.113736.338 [<ideas.........] |---|---|---|---|
20260529.113736.967 [<ideas.........] | `## KPOP_SOLVED` is emitted only after all gates truly pass | Agent writes the marker the moment clippy is clean, before
20260529.113737.541 [<ideas.........] the tail finishes | Marker is never written until malvin's gate runner confirms | Marker written while `make test` / `cargo
20260529.113738.102 [<ideas.........] nextest` children are still alive (10 procs, ~1 GiB RSS in sandbox logs) |
20260529.113738.817 [<ideas.........] | Malvin and agent evaluate the same gate proposition | Every checks line runs to completion on every verification | Malvin
20260529.113739.633 [<ideas.........] uses fail-fast prefix; agent uses one bundled shell pipeline | `make test` takes ~115s; post-`KPOP_SOLVED` malvin verdict
20260529.113739.840 [<ideas.........] must fit in ~3s |
20260529.113740.954 [<ideas.........] | `cargo clippy` is a property of source files | Clippy is evaluated over all `--all-targets` artifact graphs | Clippy
20260529.113741.176 [<ideas.........] outcome depends on which shell/cwd compiled which crate set | `cd rust &&` in `.malvin/checks` vs agent's persistent `rust/`
20260529.113741.224 [<ideas.........] cwd from prior tool calls |
20260529.113741.771 [<ideas.........] | Sandbox session end means workspace quiescence | All child processes are dead before malvin rechecks | Children outlive
20260529.113742.161 [<ideas.........] the ACP session | `Blocking waiting for file lock on artifact directory` during overlapping `cargo` invocations |
20260529.113742.721 [<ideas.........] | `quality_gates.log` is the audit trail | Every malvin gate run appends there | Post-session rechecks leave no log artifact
20260529.113743.437 [<ideas.........] | Next agent reads empty log, infers "malvin never re-ran gates," chases the wrong failure mode |
20260529.113743.456 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.113743.797 [<ideas.........] ## Idea 1: Premature `KPOP_SOLVED` collides with sandbox cargo-lock tail
20260529.113744.358 [<ideas.........] **Structural move:** Treat `## KPOP_SOLVED` not as "gates passed" but as "agent believes the hard part is done" — and let
20260529.113745.013 [<ideas.........] malvin's post-session recheck fire while the sandbox still holds live `cargo`/`nextest`/`pytest` children from the agent's
20260529.113745.189 [<ideas.........] own verification run.
20260529.113745.772 [<ideas.........] **Assumption pushed:** Session end is instantaneous and the workspace is idle. At the extreme, the agent appends
20260529.113746.338 [<ideas.........] `KPOP_SOLVED` to the exp log (~11:27:05 edit) while the 128s bundled gate command is still running; sandbox telemetry shows
20260529.113747.022 [<ideas.........] ~986 MiB RSS and 10 processes through ~11:27:23. Malvin's independent `cd rust && cargo clippy` then enters the same
20260529.113747.449 [<ideas.........] `target/` lock graph the agent's tests are still holding (logs already show `Blocking waiting for file lock on artifact
20260529.113747.469 [<ideas.........] directory`).
20260529.113748.188 [<ideas.........] **Negation explored:** Malvin waits for sandbox RSS to hit zero and all `/proc` children to exit before any
20260529.113748.759 [<ideas.........] post-`KPOP_SOLVED` gate line runs. Idea 1 is the opposite pole: malvin rechecks immediately on session teardown into a
20260529.113749.156 [<ideas.........] contested lock graph.
20260529.113749.564 [<ideas.........] **Pathological scaling:** As `make test` grows (662 pytest + 271 nextest here), the tail of concurrent build/test processes
20260529.113750.063 [<ideas.........] lengthens; the probability that malvin's clippy gate overlaps that tail approaches 1 even when source fixes are already on
20260529.113750.081 [<ideas.........] disk.
20260529.113750.684 [<ideas.........] **Observable split:** Agent's bundled run eventually exits 0 and reports all gates green; malvin's clippy-only recheck
20260529.113751.249 [<ideas.........] within ~3s exits non-zero → retry banner, despite identical source tree moments later.
20260529.113751.258 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.113751.651 [<ideas.........] ## Idea 2: Fail-fast prefix oracle vs bundled 128-second proof obligation
20260529.113752.095 [<ideas.........] **Structural move:** Malvin and the agent are not checking the same logical formula. Malvin executes `.malvin/checks` as a
20260529.113752.434 [<ideas.........] sequential, short-circuit program (one fresh shell per line, stop on first failure). The agent executes a single chained
20260529.113752.627 [<ideas.........] shell command that must survive the entire tail.
20260529.113753.158 [<ideas.........] **Assumption pushed:** Every gate verification runs all four lines to completion. At the extreme, malvin's
20260529.113753.818 [<ideas.........] post-`KPOP_SOLVED` decision must render before spawning g2 — here only ~3.4 seconds elapse between g1's `KPOP_LOG` and g2's
20260529.113754.274 [<ideas.........] prompt. That interval cannot contain `make test` (~115s in this repo). Therefore malvin's retry verdict is necessarily
20260529.113754.762 [<ideas.........] computed on a **prefix** of `.malvin/checks` (kiss → ruff → clippy at most), never the full file.
20260529.113755.187 [<ideas.........] **Negation explored:** Malvin blocks the outer loop until the entire checks file finishes, including `make test`, before
20260529.113755.775 [<ideas.........] deciding whether to retry. Idea 2's pole is the opposite: the loop may advance on a prefix verdict while the tail is still
20260529.113756.031 [<ideas.........] logically unobserved.
20260529.113756.660 [<ideas.........] **Pathological edge:** Initial malvin run already demonstrated prefix behavior — clippy failed at line 3, so `make test` was
20260529.113757.287 [<ideas.........] never run by malvin on that pass. The agent's "all four gates pass" claim is a **strictly stronger** proposition (128s
20260529.113757.741 [<ideas.........] bundled proof). Malvin retries because its weaker prefix proposition failed or was never re-evaluated to completion, not
20260529.113757.911 [<ideas.........] because the agent lied about the bundle it eventually finished.
20260529.113758.641 [<ideas.........] **Empty log amplifies this:** With `quality_gates.log` at 0 bytes, g2 cannot see which prefix line malvin actually re-ran;
20260529.113758.824 [<ideas.........] it only sees the retry reason string baked into the prompt.
20260529.113758.864 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.113759.278 [<ideas.........] ## Idea 3: `cd rust &&` clippy is a different formal gate than the agent's clippy
20260529.113800.227 [<ideas.........] **Structural move:** Line 3 of `.malvin/checks` is not the symbol `cargo clippy` — it is the composite command `cd rust &&
20260529.113800.421 [<ideas.........] cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings -W clippy::cargo` run from repo root in a fresh shell. The agent's
20260529.113800.891 [<ideas.........] sandbox session accumulates cwd, incremental cache, and prior `cargo` invocations across tool calls.
20260529.113801.427 [<ideas.........] **Assumption pushed:** Clippy outcome is a function of source text only. At the extreme, clippy outcome is a function of
20260529.113802.276 [<ideas.........] (source × cwd × incremental artifact graph × which targets were already built). The g1 fix used `#[cfg(test)]` on
20260529.113802.641 [<ideas.........] `faiss_pool_might_need_escalation` — under `-D warnings` with `--all-targets`, dead_code visibility depends on which crate
20260529.113802.909 [<ideas.........] profiles get compiled in which order.
20260529.113803.318 [<ideas.........] **Negation explored:** There is no `cd rust &&` prefix; clippy is always invoked from a single canonical working directory
20260529.113803.965 [<ideas.........] shared by malvin and agent. Idea 3 negates that: malvin always re-roots into `rust/` per line; the agent often never leaves
20260529.113804.184 [<ideas.........] `rust/` after the first `cargo` tool call.
20260529.113804.805 [<ideas.........] **Pathological edge:** Two clippy runs on identical files return different exit codes because one run sees a cold `cd rust
20260529.113805.419 [<ideas.........] &&` shell with a stale or locked `target/` directory while the other reuses a warm agent session that already compiled test
20260529.113806.027 [<ideas.........] targets. This is not a parameter tweak (`-D warnings` is the same); it is a **shell-state fork** in the same formal lint
20260529.113806.046 [<ideas.........] system.
20260529.113806.764 [<ideas.........] **Checks-file drift (same family, further pole):** If `.malvin/checks` was modified mid-run (g2 noted clippy was added to
20260529.113807.119 [<ideas.........] the file), the agent may have validated against the prompt-embedded gate list while malvin rechecked against the on-disk
20260529.113807.424 [<ideas.........] file at session end — two specifications in one loop.
20260529.113807.444 [<ideas.........] ---
20260529.113807.474 [<ideas.........] ## tl;dr
20260529.113808.022 [<ideas.........] Three structurally different explanations, all inside malvin's gate-loop rules: (1) malvin rechecks clippy while the agent's
20260529.113808.635 [<ideas.........] sandbox still holds cargo/test children and file locks, so malvin fails a gate the agent's later bundled run passes; (2)
20260529.113809.133 [<ideas.........] malvin's ~3s post-`KPOP_SOLVED` verdict can only evaluate a fail-fast prefix of `.malvin/checks` (through clippy), not the
20260529.113809.735 [<ideas.........] full 128s proof including `make test`; (3) malvin's `cd rust && cargo clippy` in fresh shells is a different proposition
20260529.113810.384 [<ideas.........] than the agent's persistent-session clippy, especially for `--all-targets` + `#[cfg(test)]` lint visibility.
